\newlabel{fig:sensor_setup}{{1}{4}{Sensor placement for data acquisition. Bipolar surface-EMG electrode pairs were positioned over the temporalis (EMG-T) and masseter (EMG-M) muscles. A microphone (MIC) was secured near the temporomandibular joint as an annotation aid; it is not analysed in this study, for the measured reasons given in Section~\ref {sec:mic}. This arrangement was evaluated only during instructed awake laboratory tasks}{figure.1}{}}
