\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces t-SNE visualisation of the 32-dimensional learned penultimate representation for held-out windows, coloured by experimental class. Chewing occupies large separate regions and rest forms tight compact islands, whereas clenching and instructed grinding interleave and movement scatters along class borders. Embeddings were recomputed from the saved fold checkpoints using only outer-test windows of one seed, so each held-out window appears exactly once.}}{17}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tsne}{{8}{17}{t-SNE visualisation of the 32-dimensional learned penultimate representation for held-out windows, coloured by experimental class. Chewing occupies large separate regions and rest forms tight compact islands, whereas clenching and instructed grinding interleave and movement scatters along class borders. Embeddings were recomputed from the saved fold checkpoints using only outer-test windows of one seed, so each held-out window appears exactly once}{figure.8}{}}
